# 15. DATA AND AI QUALITY RULES

- Every dataset must have a source URL.
- Every dataset must have an identifiable license or be marked as license-unverified and blocked from ingestion.
- Record attribution requirements.
- Record collection date and dataset version.
- Do not scrape private or restricted data.
- Do not use personal data without a lawful, documented basis.
- Do not ingest secrets or credentials.
- Do not treat model-generated text as verified facts.
- Every RAG answer must cite retrieved sources when source-backed claims are made.
- Every financial insight must be calculated from actual records.
- Every AI action must be permission-checked.
- Every agent run must be logged.
- Every scheduled action must be cancellable.
- Every consequential external action must require the relevant approval.

